Required interpretation
This is the first real-provider Full WOW v1.2 live observation where both Local DRS v0.2 and AVF v0.2 are visible inside the live multi-LLM/fractal lane.

DRS v0.2 remembers, links, and warns. It does not decide, does not grant permission, and creates only local proof/audit writeback after the Root boundary.

AVF v0.2 consumes bounded DRS candidate/reuse/risk signals, applies advisory pressure/ranking, hard-masks unsafe routes, and allows safe candidates to rank without permission. AVF v0.2 does not decide, does not grant permission, does not create truth, does not create FinalOutput, does not create ActionCommitPacket, does not create receipt, does not execute payment, does not release shipment, and cannot bypass Root.

Root remains final authority.

Audit conclusion
The AVF v0.2 + Full WOW v1.2 live observation real-provider run is PASS. The run used six real provider calls in the existing live multi-LLM/fractal lane, made Local DRS v0.2 and AVF v0.2 visible before Orchestrator, carried bounded AVF/DRS-informed context through BSEP, preserved branch advisory semantics, reached Root boundary, and produced no action, receipt, payment, shipment, FinalOutput-by-AVF, production persistence, public-auditor readiness claim, or real-world effects.
